; examples-tracker harness, the READ half. `song.it` is a SYMLINK to
; `examples/tracker/piece.it` — the committed artifact, not a fixture
; `zig build fixtures` generates. Its bytes come from one command, which
; `examples/tracker/README.md` names and `examples-tracker`'s golden
; re-runs; the `(fixture …)` line below pins them by hash, so an artifact
; regenerated from a changed document, or never regenerated at all, fails
; here.
;
; `(read)` and `(roundtrip)` are the format core's two rungs over a file
; tempura wrote: the header, the orders, the patterns and the
; pass-through regions, then `write(read(bytes)) == bytes` and a field-
; for-field re-read. The `TMPU` chunk is a trailing region and the
; message tail is the message, so both carriers ride through the rungs as
; the file's own bytes.
;
; `(walk)` is the tracker's own state machine over this module: one row
; per row played, the tempo segments the `Txx` at row 32 makes, and the
; loop point `:end loop` asked for.
;
; The `(echo …)` block every case opens with is the same walk seen as a
; TimeMap. (The `(timing)` directive the harness manifest declares is
; UNRUN in this build: the `timing` verb and `tpr_timing` went with the
; studio provider, and the echo says what they would have.)
;
; `(dump)` is the other end of the round trip `examples-tracker` asserts:
; the timeline tier reconciled out of these bytes alone, printed in full.
; A reviewer reads it against `examples/tracker/piece.sjon`.
(read)
(roundtrip)
(walk)
(dump)
